  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Network and access",
      "items": [
        "All 23 listed containers belong to the documented Proxmox homelab; the bridge boundary groups their LAN placement.",
        "Pi-hole supplies DNS only. Caddy handles reverse proxying; exact upstreams and public exposure are undocumented.",
        "WireGuard has LAN address 192.168.0.217 and tunnel interface 10.0.0.1/24."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Storage",
      "items": [
        "TrueNAS media is mounted on Proxmox and passed into Jellyfin; the mount protocol is not recorded.",
        "Jellyfin transcodes use /vault. The local ZFS mirror has two 12 TB disks on native SATA.",
        "A relationship between TrueNAS, /vault and the local ZFS pool is not established in the source."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Snapshot, not a live probe",
      "items": [
        "16 running + 7 stopped containers. Unknown DHCP addresses remain unknown.",
        "Runtime facts come from docs/container-mapping.md and docs/architecture.md; states and IPs can change.",
        "No application dependencies are inferred from names. Monitoring's live internal stack is not recorded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "How infrastructure is managed",
      "items": [
        "CI validates Terraform and Ansible. Deployment is manually dispatched on a self-hosted runner.",
        "Terraform declares Proxmox LXC resources; optional Ansible runs the site playbook after the Terraform job.",
        "Declarations and Ansible inventory differ from the runtime snapshot; application tasks are partly unimplemented."
      ]
    }
  ]
